Z||000010||Fiero Sam||08-15-2001||06:22 PM||||I drive my Fiero because I love my Fiero.And because I can't afford another car.If I were to win $100,000,000 in the lottery,I would start looking for a second Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000011||starfighter007@msn.com||08-15-2001||06:34 PM||||Well I probobly could afford to get much more expensive car.I gotta tell though my little baby is pretty comfortable on long drives easy to maintain fun to drive.It may not be the fastest car on the road but she keeps up with traffic.Other than the speed thing.For me that would be a dumb finacial move.||||reg||10
Z||000012||WampusCat||08-15-2001||07:07 PM||||I bought a new BMW 323i with every option except automatic in '98 and had it paid off in 9 months.  When I got married, my wife couldn't drive the 5-sp, so we sold it and got her an auto.  She now has a '01 Volvo S40(that I get to pay for) and I split my driving between the Fiero and my '92 Toyota PU that I bought used in '96.  The Fiero is just as much fun to drive as the 323, just not as refined and quiet.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cheever3000||08-15-2001||07:43 PM||||Shoot yeah, there's <I>lots</I> of nice sporty cars I'd rather have if I had the dough! <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Songman||08-15-2001||07:56 PM||||I don't know anything about that other thread but that is just crazy! I've had some of the best cars ever built (and some expensive ones that weren't so great!) and I still own Fieros. Money has nothing to do with why I like my Fieros.<P>I've had 3 911 Porsches (2 Targas), a Jaguar XJS, a Corvette, a Lexus, and a ton of other cars. I drive what I like and money has nothing to do with it. People used to look at me funny when I would ride around in my 69 Judge because they didn't know what it was. I drove it because I loved it even though I had more comfortable cars at home.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||maryjane||08-15-2001||09:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR>In other words, who is driving a Fiero because they really want to, versus that is all they could afford?[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>All they could afford?<BR>I don't know about anybody else, but there are any number of cars I could own and afford easier than a 17 yr old Fiero. Keeping an older sports car up & running ain't exactly cheap!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Raydar||08-15-2001||09:45 PM||||If I had more disposable income, I'd just have a nicer Fiero. <BR>Biggest problem I have is space to keep everything. We have my wife's Wrangler, my Sonoma, and 2 1/2 Fieros.<BR>Almost bought a new Sonoma, but I decided to have my A/C fixed and give it a paint job and a new set of wheels, instead. <BR>Next car will probably either be a GP or an Acura 3.2 TL. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000017||rogergarrison||08-15-2001||10:05 PM||||I like Ferrari's. I could afford a real one but chose to build the replica instead. Mine actually outperforms the real one now. If I had had a million to spare Id like a REAL Ford GT-40. Its just a small block Ford engine so I could work on it myself too, just like the Fiero. (and no computer crap) Id prob still have the Fiero/Ferrari to play around in too.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Neal||08-15-2001||11:22 PM||||Lots of cars id like to own but here are a few<BR>under 50,000<BR>fiero (i own one but i really do like em)<BR>highly modded fiero<BR>3rd gen RX-7<BR>2002 camaro SS<BR>subaru SVX or the WRX<P>over 50,000<BR>Z06 vette<BR>BMW M3<BR>a NEW maserati<P>those are the important ones||||reg||1
Z||000019||Standard||08-15-2001||11:23 PM||||Well.. if I had money... I would probably have a Porsche 944 Turbo, or if I had alot of money a 928 GTS.. or a new Trans Am, or Grand Prix GTP...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000020||72vinman||08-15-2001||11:40 PM||||I am not sure I agree. I am doing very well for myself these days. Other than some of the exotic sports cars I could probably afford any car I desired. However, I purchase what I feel is practical. I put a lot of miles on my cars right now because of my job. So instead of blowing my money I drive a 97 sunfire. Did not cost a lot to buy and does not cost a lot to maintain. My wife really wanted a minivan so she could see over the other cars on the road so we bought a Windstar. <BR>I bought my Fiero not because I had to but because I really love the way they look and drive. The fact that they are cheaper than a Ferrari is just an added bonus.<BR>That is my $.02<P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Black 86GT||||reg||3
Z||000021||kslish||08-16-2001||03:25 AM||||I drive my Fiero(s) because I love the cars.  I'll probably always have one (or more).  It's sort of a hobby for me.  What kind of money I have is irrelavant, and anyone who knows me knows that I don't pinch pennies or anything like that.  I've just been hooked on the Fiero since 1988 (started young with my Dad's).<P>I just get a kick out of driving unique cars....but I don't understand how anyone can stereotype Fiero owners and such to a particular class of society.  That old guy in the nice old MGB in the lane next to you on the highway could be scraping by on his Social Security checks or he could be a multi millionaire.  The same should apply to Fieros. <P>Now if I hit the Powerball lotto, and cost was no object...there are some cars I would like to add to my GM "orphan collection":<P>Buick Reatta - I will own one of these as soon as I can find one in decent shape for sale.  It has to be in good shape because some parts for this car make looking for rare Fiero parts seem REALLY easy.  <P>Cadillac Allante - It would make a good interstate cruiser for weekend trips.  <P>2002 Firebird - I may end up getting one of these anyways, but haven't decided on it for sure.  <P>Yes I do have a somewhat odd taste in cars....and I'm still thinking too practical with naming stuff I could probably buy now anyways, let me think harder.....<P>There would be some other stuff thrown in there too.  I'd probably have a Nissan Skyline GT-R imported for me....some various models from Italy, that Ford GT-40 that Roger mentioned would be nice to go vintage racing with.  A DeTamaso Pantera would be somewhere on my list also, as well as a Lotus Esprit.<P>Oh yeah, forgot to mention the Datsun 240Z that I always wanted also.  One of the ones from the 70's before the later Z's got all heavy and bloated in the early to mid 80's.  But again, that's another car that is still pretty affordable.<P>There are other cars that I'm probably forgetting.  <P>Basically, I won't buy a car I don't like....and I like my cars to be special in some way.  The Fiero does it for me.<P>Ken S.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000022||artherd||08-16-2001||04:26 AM||||Ok, if form some *INSANE* reason I had literally unlimited funds, but could only own one car due to some completely implausable restriction.....<P>I'd drop the fiero in a second and buy a Ferrari F355 Spyder. I know the colour too.<P>Of course, this is the ONLY car I would ever trade my fiero for. (and it would have to come with a great deal of cash in the boot as well.)<P>Ok, maybe a 1994 512TR.  Maybe.  <P>And maaaaybe if the right 288GTO came along.<P>Possibly for a perfect 328. I mean perfect.  No, probally not for the 328. (ok, maybe.  aagh!!!)<P>I'm a ferrari nut, and I actually thinking I'm driving the cheapest Ferrari Enzo ever made, he just had GM build it for him :)<P><BR>In this universe, I'm putting a manual tranny Northstar in my t-top Formula right now, and someday I'll have that F355 Spyder *TOO*.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000023||Raydar||08-16-2001||10:39 AM||||If I ever hit the Lotto (fat chance)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">, I'll keep the Fieros, but I'll buy a Ferrari 360 Modena. And enough garage space for all of 'em.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000024||DRH||08-16-2001||01:11 PM||||One reason I have the Fiero is so I CAN work on it. If I struck it rich I would probably just do more exotic changes to a Fiero. There are a lot of possibilities; Northstar, Finale kit, BIG brakes, suspension, etc... ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Wolfhound||08-16-2001||01:33 PM||||I think DRH hit the nail on the head, for me, at any rate. Half the fun is working on the cars. Driving a car you brought up to speed is much more meaningful than crusing around and making monster car payments. I enjoy the fact that for very little money I can alter and change this little car that almost all parts are interchangeable on.<BR> I get real involved with my projects and can hardly wait to get back to them when I'm away.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Steve Normington||08-16-2001||03:33 PM||||I'd probably get a MR2 Spyder and a 60's Mach 1 to go along with my Fiero. ||||reg||1
Z||000027||wkayl||08-16-2001||04:18 PM||||Ok, here is my 2 cents worth.  I own a Fiero because in 1986 the company I work for gave one away exactly like mine (except for it had no A/C).  I own 2 other collector cars, a 1967 Buick Skylark conv. and a 1961 Studebaker Lark XIII.  If I won the lottery I would also have a Viper, Prowler, and a Vett.  Last fall I bought a new 2001 Chev Silverado  ext. cab shortbed 4X4.  I could just as well bought a used truck and a used Vett.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000028||fierobaby||08-16-2001||04:23 PM||||put it this way from my point yes I could have afforded a nicer car but I fell in love with this little red plastic thing with wheels... so I got it... its a great car and even if I could have gotten or found something nicer which I did... I wouldn't have gotten it I would have gotten a nice Green ford Tarus... but nope my little red baby is awesome! but lets say I did win the lottery I would get a VW Jetta in electric blue... I knwo you're all thinking why buy that they are some cute cars!<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="LETTER"> AIM: Fierobaby87 <A HREF="http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero" TARGET=_blank>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</A>  </FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
